The Bucket Auto Strategy employs MongoDB’s `$bucketAuto` aggregation stage to intelligently partition documents into a specified number of buckets based on the `_id` field.

OLake Go constructs an aggregation pipeline using `$sort` and `$bucketAuto`, where the number of buckets is set to `4` times the configured maximum number of threads. Each bucket returned by MongoDB contains a range (`min`, `max`) of `_id` values and a document count. These ranges are then used for parallel processing.

